       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Nothing in the details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify going above that. At this dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding effects.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **200 mg once daily**, the maximum dose.\n- **A lower dose.** The usual start is 25\u201350 mg daily, titrated by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least a week. Depression, OCD, and PTSD typically use 50\u2013200 mg/day.\n- **400 mg is intentional.** This would be unusual, so tell me the indication and rationale. I can enter it with a note such as \"dose exceeds labeled max, confirmed with attending/pharmacy.\" I'd recommend checking with pharmacy or your attending first.\n\nTell me which one you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
